      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I might have found out why VRChat is having problem right now.\n\nI just found out a week ago that VRChat had an encryption update at the end of March, thus \"permanently\" putting an end to the ripping crisis. But that also messes up VRChat itself because encrypted files/data are gonna do nothing but cause problems.\n\nThe files/data that makes the game operate needs to be non-encrypted in order to make it run properly, otherwise most of the used assets will have noticeable glitchy appearance, prevent people from downloading in-game files (avatars, worlds), and it will start crashing a lot.\n\nThese screenshots I've made over a month ago and present are great examples.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
