      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I'm not sure if I have to create a new post talking about this issue some users like me are experiencing right now because this post is still marked as 'Tracked' ever since it was posted, but this issue has been active for 10 months now.\n\nI believe this encryption update needs to be reverted or at least heavily optimized because there are modded clients out there that can easily decrypt files, which means encrypted files did nothing but caused more problems inside VRChat, as shown in the screenshots I provided, than it did with preventing rippers.\n\nNow, when I said this encryption update needs to be reverted, I'm not saying I'm encouraging ripping because I don't mean it like that, so please do not start jumping to conclusions. I just think it didn't do anything and it only made VRChat itself unplayable for some users.\n\nThere's a custom VRC Anti-Rip component called Kanna Protecc, which is a component that can prevent the avatar from being ripped, sort of. I'll provide the link if you want to check it out. ---> https://github.com/PlagueVRC/AntiRip\n\nBut if you don't want people using custom components to prevent avatars from being ripped, then my only suggestion I have right now is make it to where avatar and world cache are immediately deleted after your device is finished loading the cache.\n\nBut I might had discovered that, and it's just a guess, when VRChat realizes the world cache isn't there anymore, then you're sent to your homeworld within 10 - 30 minutes. For example, I stay in an Optimized Box or YouTube Search for too long, the cache of either worlds I'm in gets deleted, and 10 minutes later, I get disconnected with an error message saying 'DisconnectedForReasonsUnknown'.\n\nI have nothing else to say, but I just hope this issue gets fixed very VERY soon because it has been active for 10 months now.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
